  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x-2y+19 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x & =2y-19 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9 & =2y-19 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =2y-19+9 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =2y-10 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =2(y-5) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})(y-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(3,5).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
